| Reverse: (0.3.10, vcdec 0.4.10) as Reel Edit plays backwards: 15 runs,
| each from a keyframe to the end with the EOS sent, 20 pictures taken,
| then a flush (the decoder created again each time), then the close,
| timed. hd and small vcdec's way, then hd the old way (-W, as devkit
| 0.2.18). A close over 50 cs is reported as SLOW. Reports to ResultR.
| (a GCCSDK program: needs SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport loaded)
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error This needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error This needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
WimpSlot -min 16384K -max 16384K
Remove <Obey$Dir>.ResultR
Run <Obey$Dir>.vcdectest -L 15 -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultR <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.mp4 <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.crc <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.sig
Run <Obey$Dir>.vcdectest -L 15 -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultR <Obey$Dir>.clips.small.mp4 <Obey$Dir>.clips.small.crc <Obey$Dir>.clips.small.sig
Run <Obey$Dir>.vcdectest -W -L 15 -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultR <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.mp4 <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.crc <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.sig
